    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Cerence Inc. describes itself as delivering conversational and agentic AI-powered user experiences for automotive and beyond. Its CaLLM family of language models is presented as enabling natural, multimodal, and safe interactions. The company also describes applications for automotive dealerships and industrial AI.\n\nThe company's Cerence EVD product uses Audio AI to detect emergency vehicles. According to the company, EVD is already deployed in production vehicles and can detect more than 1,500 emergency sirens across nearly 50 countries. It can identify approaching emergency vehicles from more than 300 meters away with interior microphones and beyond 800 meters when paired with exterior microphones. Cerence reported third quarter results with revenue up 12% YoY, connected services revenue up 20% YoY, and operating cash flow of $20M supporting a first-ever share repurchase program. The company also describes work with Microsoft on Zero Trust and layered AI security for in-car assistants.\n\nCerence Inc. is a for-profit public company headquartered in Burlington, Massachusetts, trading under ticker CRNC with SEC CIK 0001768267. Massachusetts legal exposure records show 191 entries under the name Cerence Inc.",
